  "hindi": "त्रिकद्रुकों में महान् और अत्यन्त बलवान् ने तृप्त होकर जौ से मिला, विष्णु के साथ निचोड़ा हुआ सोम, जैसी इच्छा हुई वैसा पिया। वह उससे बड़ा कर्म करने के लिए हर्षित हुआ। उस महान् और विशाल देव, सत्य इन्द्र का वह देव, सत्य इन्दु अनुसरण करे।",
  "english": "In the Trikadrukas the mighty one, very strong, delighted, drank the Soma mixed with barley, pressed with Viṣṇu, as he wished. He rejoiced in it to do a great action. May the true drop, a god, attend him, the great and wide, the god, the true Indra.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The subject of line 1 is not named; Indra is clear from the refrain. trikadruka is left as a plural place or rite name. viṣṇunā sutam: 'pressed with Viṣṇu' (inst.; 'by Viṣṇu' is also possible). īm taken as 'it' (the Soma); 'him' is also possible. mahām urum is taken with enam (him). The refrain 'sa enaṃ saścad ...' recurs in each verse of this hymn; the printed token sainaṃ is saḥ enam. induḥ 'drop' (a name of Soma).",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
