  "hindi": "तुम संकल्प के साथ उत्पन्न हुए, बल के साथ तुम बढ़े; वीर कर्मों के साथ बढ़ा हुआ तुम शत्रुओं को पराभूत करने वाले और सब ओर देखने वाले हो। तुम स्तुति करने वाले को वाञ्छित धन और दान के देने वाले हो। उस देव, सत्य इन्द्र का वह देव, सत्य इन्दु अनुसरण करे।",
  "english": "Together with resolve you were born, together with might you grew strong; together with heroic deeds grown great, you are the overcomer of foes, all-surveying. You are the giver of bounty, of desirable wealth, to the praiser. May the true drop, a god, attend him, the god, the true Indra.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "vavakṣitha taken as 2 sg. perfect of √vakṣ 'grow strong'. The sentence has no stated finite verb for the second half, so 'you are' is supplied only to make the clauses read as one statement (the epithets are nominatives). vicarṣaṇi is uncertain ('all-surveying'; also 'surpassing, active'). mṛdhaḥ taken as accusative plural 'foes' (mṛdh 'enemy, hostility'). The person shifts between 'you' and 'him' (refrain). Refrain as in unit 1.",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
